<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  android:fullBackupContent - Auto Backup on API 24-30 (G6b P3b, P5).

  Excludes the Last.fm files and nothing else. A rule file with only <exclude>
  elements keeps the default of backing up everything not excluded, so every other
  file - the Supabase session and myata_database included - is backed up exactly
  as it was before this file existed. Widening this is a separate decision.

  Why exclude them:
   - `lastfm_session` holds the listener's Last.fm session key, which lives until
     they revoke it. Restored onto another device, or out of a cloud backup, it
     would scrobble as them from a phone they never linked. It also holds the
     pending request token, which is useless anywhere but the device that asked.
   - `lastfm_queue` (P5) holds scrobbles waiting to be sent. Restored elsewhere they
     would be sent from there too, duplicating what this device already sent. It is
     a Room database, so its write-ahead log and shared-memory files go with it.
  - `myata_playback_intent` (playback process-death recovery) holds which station
     was last selected and whether the listener wanted it playing. It is runtime
     state about one device's speaker: restored onto a new phone it would mean an
    app that has never played anything believing it was mid-broadcast, and the
    first thing the system restarted could be a radio the owner never started
    there. Nothing is lost by dropping it - a fresh device has nothing to recover.
   - `myata_playback_commands` (the durable command inbox) holds gestures this
     device's listener has made and the service has not handled yet. Same reason,
     one step stronger: restored onto another device it is an instruction nobody
     gave there, and the first service start would carry it out.
   - `myata_sleep_timer_undo` (what `Вернуть` would put back) holds the timer as it
     was at the moment it was cancelled. It is one device's gesture too, and on
     another device it would offer to restore a countdown that was never running
     there. Its deadline is monotonic, so it is also inert anywhere but the boot it
     was measured on.

  Keep the paths in step with PrefsLastfmSessionStore.FILE,
  LastfmQueueDatabase.FILE, PlaybackIntentStore.FILE, PlaybackCommandInbox.FILE,
  SleepTimerStore.UNDO_FILE and lastfm_data_extraction_rules.xml.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="lastfm_session.xml" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="lastfm_queue" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="lastfm_queue-wal" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="lastfm_queue-shm" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="myata_playback_intent.xml" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="myata_playback_commands.xml" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="myata_sleep_timer_undo.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
